sysrepo
------------------------------------------
Sysrepo is a YANG-based configuration and operational state data store for
Unix/Linux applications.

Runtime requirements:
  bash-5.2.21-1
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libsysrepo-devel-5.2.27-1bl1
  libsysrepo8-5.2.27-1bl1
  libyang-devel-6.4.13-1bl2
  libyang5-6.4.13-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libcmocka-devel-2.0.2-1
  libyang-devel-6.4.13-1bl2
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/sysrepo/sysrepo

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/sysrepo/sysrepo/archive/refs/tags/v5.2.27.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack sysrepo-5.2.27-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./sysrepo-5.2.27-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/sysrepo-5.2.27-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/sysrepo-5.2.27-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsysrepo8-5.2.27-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsysrepo-devel-5.2.27-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

